## Summary

**pain.001.001.11 mapping**
- `DbtrAgtAcct` is now mapped from the payer bank's account number
- `InitgPty` uses the payer when the payload names no initiating party (`HeaderRules.initiatingPartyFallback`, default `PAYER`)
- The field that fills `UETR` is chosen by rule (`IdentifierRules.uetrSource`)
- `PayloadPreconditions` checks the charge bearer when it is present
- Golden XML samples refreshed for the above

**XML to FIS JSON (new package `fis`)**
- `FisJsonConverter` turns the pain.001.001.11 message into the FIS request JSON in memory, after checking it against the XSD
- JSON names come from `pain001-v11-fis-names.json`, built from the XSD and the FIS contract by the `generateFisNameTable` task
- `WirePaymentFisJson` goes from the Base64 payment object to the FIS JSON in one call
- A failure throws `FisJsonConversionException` with every problem listed; no partial message is returned
- Output is deterministic: same input, same bytes
- `build.gradle`: adds `jackson-databind`, `json-schema-validator` (tests only) and the tasks `renderFisJson` and `generateFisNameTable`


- [x] `./gradlew test` passes (122 tests)
- [x] Golden JSON of all 8 samples validates against the FIS contract
- [x] FIS's own sample requests convert back to the same JSON
- [x] `./gradlew renderFisJson` writes the samples to `build/samples/fis-json`
